1
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:24,733
Welcome to the Island of Affection.

2
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:25,200
Hello.

3
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:25,833
Hello.

4
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:26,733
I'm afraid to go over.

5
00:00:26,733 --> 00:00:27,966
Very happy.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,466
I'm leaving.

7
00:00:28,466 --> 00:00:28,933
Not to answer...

8
00:00:29,666 --> 00:00:30,600
Hello.

9
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:32,166
Do you believe in love at first sight?

10
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,666
Affection only for you.

11
00:00:33,666 --> 00:00:34,900
So this is mutual.

12
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:35,433
Bye-bye.

13
00:00:35,466 --> 00:00:39,200
[Day 11]

14
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,400
[One Missing Piece.
Just Like a Heart Falling in Love]

15
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:42,866
I think I like you.

16
00:00:42,866 --> 00:00:46,500
We could even hold hands here
on the island, be together.

17
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:47,333
Do we need

18
00:00:47,333 --> 00:00:49,200
to go through more things together

19
00:00:49,233 --> 00:00:50,700
to really get to know each other?

20
00:00:50,733 --> 00:00:52,333
[One Step Shy of Experience]

21
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:54,133
I don't know

22
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,400
what life after this will be like.

23
00:00:55,433 --> 00:00:56,300
It's unpredictable.

24
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,933
I hope in real life we can be like

25
00:00:59,933 --> 00:01:01,266
we are here on the island.

26
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,166
But I like living in the moment.

27
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,033
[A Breath Away from Tomorrow]

28
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:07,700
Why are you nervous?

29
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,366
I'm not sure.

30
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,333
Let's see tomorrow.

31
00:01:11,333 --> 00:01:13,800
When you go back,
don't forget me right away.

32
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,800
[A Step Away from Certainty]

33
00:01:16,633 --> 00:01:18,133
Too soon.

34
00:01:18,133 --> 00:01:19,333
Will you miss me?

35
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:21,400
I think I will.

36
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:24,033
[A Second Short of Enough Time]

37
00:01:26,666 --> 00:01:27,300
Happiness matters the most.

38
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:28,900
Doing what makes you happy

39
00:01:28,900 --> 00:01:29,533
is already enough.

40
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:37,400
[Tonight, the moon reaches its fullest.]

41
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,433
[Will our story complete its circle?]

42
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:00,833
[Love Wins All]

43
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,533
[As the final page turns,]

44
00:02:09,533 --> 00:02:12,066
[we pack our bags]
Things on the island feel like a bubble.

45
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:16,033
[and the memories we made here.]
Like another parallel world.

46
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:18,566
In real life,

47
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,933
we're bombarded

48
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:23,000
by disparate information

49
00:02:23,033 --> 00:02:27,700
coming from all directions.

50
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,900
But on this island,

51
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:30,800
I find there are so many

52
00:02:30,833 --> 00:02:33,466
beautiful things.

53
00:02:33,466 --> 00:02:34,733
[The twelve days have turned into amber,]
I'm so grateful

54
00:02:34,733 --> 00:02:36,933
[The twelve days have turned into amber,]
for these 12 days

55
00:02:36,966 --> 00:02:40,066
[glowing forever in our hearts.]
on the Island of Affection.

56
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:44,533
[Day 12 Confession Day]
Hello, Panpan.

57
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:45,833
[Today's Affection Moon Phase: Full Moon]
Today's our last day

58
00:02:45,866 --> 00:02:47,866
[Today's Affection Moon Phase: Full Moon]
on the Island of Affection.

59
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:49,966
[Today's Affection Moon Phase: Full Moon]
Time really flew by...

60
00:02:52,466 --> 00:02:55,166
Recording this makes me a bit nervous.

61
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:57,133
The camera just pointed at me.

62
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:05,366
[Every word is written carefully,]

63
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:08,866
[offering a sincere heart
for the final chapter.]

64
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,833
Take a flower

65
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:12,966
Ma gave me.

66
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,066
Are you going to get messages?

67
00:03:17,066 --> 00:03:17,733
Yeah.

68
00:03:18,866 --> 00:03:20,066
You can come find me later.

69
00:03:20,066 --> 00:03:21,500
Okay, who will you find first?

70
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:22,200
I don't know.

71
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:23,633
I'll find whoever comes up.

72
00:03:23,633 --> 00:03:25,533
Just record everyone with my DV camera.

73
00:03:25,533 --> 00:03:26,266
Ask each of them

74
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,400
to draw me a little star.

75
00:03:28,433 --> 00:03:30,100
Look at the gift I got you.

76
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,633
A bear that looks like me.

77
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,800
Susu.

78
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,200
Let me put on my earrings.

79
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,733
You look exactly the same.

80
00:03:39,733 --> 00:03:41,233
What are you writing?

81
00:03:42,233 --> 00:03:43,100
Not showing you.

82
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,433
Racking your brain.

83
00:03:44,466 --> 00:03:44,866
Not showing you.

84
00:03:44,866 --> 00:03:45,900
I'm done writing.

85
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:46,533
Yeah?

86
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:49,366
Can I sign it?

87
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,466
Go on.

88
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,400
Sign here.

89
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:53,500
Okay.

90
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,433
Sign over the heart.

91
00:03:55,466 --> 00:03:57,000
Sign over the heart.

92
00:03:57,033 --> 00:03:59,300
[Sign over the heart.]

93
00:03:59,733 --> 00:04:01,600
Then I'll make it bigger.

94
00:04:01,633 --> 00:04:02,533
I'm gonna take up the whole space.

95
00:04:02,533 --> 00:04:03,533
Not leaving you any.

96
00:04:03,533 --> 00:04:04,466
Okay.

97
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,433
Write

98
00:04:07,466 --> 00:04:09,000
'Ma Haoteng'?

99
00:04:12,233 --> 00:04:14,633
This looks terribly ugly.

100
00:04:14,633 --> 00:04:15,733
I think that'll do.

101
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:17,133
Yeah.

102
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:17,666
Good?

103
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:18,233
So be it.

104
00:04:18,266 --> 00:04:19,500
It looks good.

105
00:04:20,300 --> 00:04:23,500
Don't you think it looks like a heart?

106
00:04:23,500 --> 00:04:24,200
Have you noticed?

107
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:25,566
Oh, it does.

108
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,133
Right?

109
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:26,966
Was it intentional?

110
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,533
Right?

111
00:04:28,533 --> 00:04:29,833
Looks like a heart, right?

112
00:04:32,266 --> 00:04:33,700
Kind of. Not bad.

113
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,033
Here.

114
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:36,866
Your turn.

115
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:39,366
Then I'll write in the same spot.

116
00:04:40,433 --> 00:04:42,300
[Staring]

117
00:04:43,466 --> 00:04:44,733
What?

118
00:04:44,733 --> 00:04:45,866
Nothing.

119
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:47,100
Just want to look at you more.

120
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,133
Just want to look at you more.

121
00:04:48,133 --> 00:04:49,866
[Just want to look at you more.]

122
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:50,700
[Just want to look at you more.]
I smudged it.

123
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:51,533
[Just want to look at you more.]

124
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,700
Is it okay?

125
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:56,133
Yeah.

126
00:04:56,133 --> 00:04:57,166
You wrote right in the center.

127
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,433
No one else can sign on this shirt.

128
00:05:00,433 --> 00:05:01,666
They're not allowed to touch it.

129
00:05:03,733 --> 00:05:04,966
You're smooth.

130
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,600
Too smooth.

131
00:05:07,633 --> 00:05:08,633
Left atrium.

132
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,933
Thought of something?

133
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:12,033
I did.

134
00:05:12,066 --> 00:05:13,866
You can look when I finish.

135
00:05:13,866 --> 00:05:14,533
Don't look yet.

136
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:15,366
Okay.

137
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,366
Done.

138
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,100
Let me see.

139
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,133
Here.

140
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:21,400
Wrote something meaningful.

141
00:05:21,433 --> 00:05:22,633
Let me see.

142
00:05:22,633 --> 00:05:25,166
Let's become better adults together.

143
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,333
'Little brat.'

144
00:05:26,333 --> 00:05:27,633
[Bam]
Shut up.

145
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:29,000
[Bam]
Shut up.

146
00:05:29,033 --> 00:05:31,133
When you read it out loud,
it feels cringey.

147
00:05:33,633 --> 00:05:35,033
I finished.

148
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:36,100
Let me see what you wrote.

149
00:05:36,933 --> 00:05:38,166
Shine bright.

150
00:05:38,200 --> 00:05:38,866
Good, huh?

151
00:05:38,866 --> 00:05:39,800
Yeah.

152
00:05:43,833 --> 00:05:47,066
Do you want my amazing butterfly or not?

153
00:05:47,066 --> 00:05:48,466
If yes, you need to wait.

154
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:51,000
It'll be worth it.

155
00:05:51,933 --> 00:05:55,166
I need to learn how to draw a butterfly.

156
00:05:57,633 --> 00:05:59,633
My first butterfly ever.

157
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:06,133
You're a real artist.

158
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,400
I'm done.

159
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:18,933
"Huihui & Xiaxia".

160
00:06:19,433 --> 00:06:20,133
Ma,

161
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:21,800
write the most unserious thing
you can think of.

162
00:06:22,333 --> 00:06:24,266
What? The most handsome guy in Xinjiang?

163
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,033
When I get famous someday,

164
00:06:25,066 --> 00:06:26,066
this shirt will be worth money.

165
00:06:26,066 --> 00:06:26,766
Just you wait.

166
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,133
You'll be rich.

167
00:06:34,100 --> 00:06:35,766
Okay.

168
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,733
Smile.

169
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:37,566
Smile.

170
00:06:38,633 --> 00:06:39,433
Thanks.

171
00:06:40,333 --> 00:06:43,333
You're the only person on the island
I'm willing to call 'bro'.

172
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:46,800
I'll keep our bond in my heart.

173
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:48,900
I'm touched already.

174
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:49,433
Yeah.

175
00:06:49,466 --> 00:06:51,066
That message is sweet.

176
00:06:51,266 --> 00:06:52,466
This is a crown.

177
00:06:52,466 --> 00:06:53,866
I drew a crown in your name.

178
00:06:53,866 --> 00:06:54,700
Great.

179
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:55,033
Awesome.

180
00:06:55,066 --> 00:06:55,666
Right?

181
00:06:55,666 --> 00:06:56,800
I like it.

182
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,666
Wang Sulong's little star.

183
00:06:58,666 --> 00:07:00,133
You really get me.

184
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:00,866
This doodle is so ugly.

185
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:01,400
Who did you draw?

186
00:07:01,433 --> 00:07:02,133
Yourself?

187
00:07:02,133 --> 00:07:02,833
Excuse me?

188
00:07:02,866 --> 00:07:03,666
You said my drawing is bad

189
00:07:03,666 --> 00:07:04,400
and then said it's me?

190
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:05,100
I'm gonna be mad.

191
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,100
I'm not signing your shirt.

192
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:08,533
Never.

193
00:07:08,533 --> 00:07:09,766
Write: "Give me back Huihui."

194
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:11,433
"Give me back day-one Huihui."

195
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:14,966
Feels like graduation season.

196
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:15,800
Yeah.

197
00:07:21,466 --> 00:07:22,533
[Zhang Xuefei's Game Suit
Ma Haoxiang's Game Suit]

198
00:07:22,533 --> 00:07:24,133
[Ink and sweat on their game suits]

199
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:24,933
[form the island's own badge of honor.]

200
00:07:24,966 --> 00:07:25,833
[Pu Yanyan's Game Suit
Kelvin Wang's Game Suit]

201
00:07:25,833 --> 00:07:26,966
[Etched deep in memory, forever shining.]

202
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,066
[Duan Danhui's Game Suit
Pan Xiaoyi's Game Suit]

203
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:32,833
[Yao Qianyu's Game Suit
Sun Shuo's Game Suit]

204
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:35,766
[Kong Xichen's Game Suit
Zhang Tianlu's Game Suit]

205
00:07:35,833 --> 00:07:37,833
[Vinson's Game Suit
Xia Boyan's Game Suit]

206
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:39,266
[Jerry Wang's Game Suit]

207
00:07:39,300 --> 00:07:40,633
[Guo Zhentao's Game Suit
Autumn's Game Suit]

208
00:07:40,666 --> 00:07:42,766
I don't want to sign something random

209
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,100
or draw something sloppy and call it done.

210
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:47,600
Leaving space means
we still have chances to write more later.

211
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:51,200
[Afraid to end the story too soon,]

212
00:07:51,233 --> 00:07:53,333
[so we leave a blank space
for the promise of next time.]

213
00:07:53,400 --> 00:07:54,766
[So sleepy.]

214
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:56,233
[Go sleep.]

215
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:57,300
[Get some more sleep.]

216
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,433
I'm so sleepy.

217
00:07:58,466 --> 00:07:59,733
I can fall asleep right away.

218
00:07:59,733 --> 00:08:01,800
Let me stand here for one second,

219
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:02,300
and I'll show you.

220
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:03,433
Alright, show me.

221
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:05,533
Just like yesterday.

222
00:08:07,133 --> 00:08:08,366
You secretly filmed me.

223
00:08:08,933 --> 00:08:10,200
Had a crush on me for two years.

224
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,300
No, twenty years.

225
00:08:13,833 --> 00:08:15,066
You're pretty familiar with the place.

226
00:08:15,066 --> 00:08:16,466
Just walked right into my room.

227
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:17,700
['Twenty Years' of Self-awareness]

228
00:08:17,700 --> 00:08:18,633
['Twenty Years' of Self-awareness]
Why not?

229
00:08:18,666 --> 00:08:20,800
['Twenty Years' of Self-awareness]

230
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,266
[You rarely went to Autumn's room before,]
I changed

231
00:08:22,266 --> 00:08:23,300
[You rarely went to Autumn's room before,]
partly because

232
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:25,333
[why these last two days?]
I'm starting to like her more.

233
00:08:25,333 --> 00:08:27,000
[why these last two days?]
And also,

234
00:08:27,033 --> 00:08:29,700
it feels like she doesn't really mind me

235
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,033
going to her place.

236
00:08:31,066 --> 00:08:33,200
I think I should be brave now.

237
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:34,666
After all, moments like this

238
00:08:34,666 --> 00:08:36,766
or meeting someone

239
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:37,933
who actually makes your heart race

240
00:08:37,933 --> 00:08:39,266
don't come that easily.

241
00:08:40,233 --> 00:08:41,533
Lie down. Go to sleep.

242
00:08:48,133 --> 00:08:50,400
I've only been to Harbin in the northeast.

243
00:08:50,433 --> 00:08:51,166
Come to Dalian.

244
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:53,466
Sure.

245
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:54,766
Sure.

246
00:08:56,133 --> 00:08:57,866
I've always wanted to go to Dalian.

247
00:08:59,300 --> 00:09:01,200
Do you want this?

248
00:09:01,233 --> 00:09:01,733
[Autumn's Avatar]
What is it?

249
00:09:01,733 --> 00:09:03,366
[Autumn's Avatar]

250
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,033
I have an extra one. Actually, I have two.

251
00:09:05,033 --> 00:09:05,933
Why?

252
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:07,400
Because I lost mine before,
couldn't find it,

253
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:08,500
and then someone found it.

254
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:10,233
Then give me one.

255
00:09:10,266 --> 00:09:11,133
Give you one?

256
00:09:12,033 --> 00:09:12,933
[Feet are giving away the mood.]

257
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:13,266
Is it okay?

258
00:09:13,333 --> 00:09:14,333
[Okay.]

259
00:09:14,333 --> 00:09:15,133
Let me see.

260
00:09:15,133 --> 00:09:17,033
This one's kinda cute.

261
00:09:17,066 --> 00:09:17,500
Let me see.

262
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:23,100
Honestly, you look better in real life.

263
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:23,533
Really?

264
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,000
Okay.

265
00:09:27,433 --> 00:09:28,700
The little starfish is yours now.

266
00:09:28,700 --> 00:09:29,700
Another one?

267
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,566
You've given me so many things.

268
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:32,500
They're all 'junk' anyway.

269
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:33,933
Okay.

270
00:09:33,933 --> 00:09:34,366
Take it.

271
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,500
You'll love it.

272
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,333
Did you pack your stuff?

273
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:39,933
Yeah.

274
00:09:39,933 --> 00:09:40,866
I'm almost done.

275
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:42,700
Almost done?

276
00:09:43,866 --> 00:09:44,166
Wait.

277
00:09:44,933 --> 00:09:45,733
[Ma, Running]

278
00:09:45,733 --> 00:09:46,333
[Ma, Running]
The bear.

279
00:09:46,333 --> 00:09:46,933
[Ma, Running]

280
00:09:53,833 --> 00:09:54,300
Let's go.

281
00:09:58,433 --> 00:09:59,100
Why are you smelling it?

282
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:01,233
Feel like it.

